<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>arc_sensor</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.9">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>Generated from ARC'26 Manual v.3</name>
    <email>info@anatolianroverchallenge.com</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    Ground sensor prop used in the Anatolian Rover Challenge (ARC'26)
    Collaboration Mission, "Sensor Task" (Manual section 7.1.4.1, step 3:
    "Collect Sensors") and referenced in the technical drawing of
    section 8.7 "Sensors - Collaboration Mission" (page 48 of the manual).

    The sensor is a free-standing, partially-buried ground probe with:
      - A flexible whip antenna on top (drawn as a zig-zag spring symbol)
      - A rigid domed antenna stub of diameter 20 mm
      - A conical shoulder collar with a ring of bolt/stud heads
      - A ribbed (bellows-style) tapered housing body
      - A cylindrical base of diameter 84 mm with two vertical slot
        cutouts, which is the portion buried/seated in the regolith
      - Total height: 190 mm
      - Height from the top of the shoulder collar to the base: 148 mm
      - Base diameter: 84 mm (radius 42 mm)
      - Antenna stub diameter: 20 mm

    All dimensions were taken directly from the dimensioned technical
    drawing in the manual (values in millimetres, converted to metres
    here per SDF convention).
  </description>
</model>
